.TH SECRET 1 "November 2025" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
.B secret 
\- transfer encrypted files over ICMP/ICMPv6 messages using a custom protocol

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B secret
\-r <file> \-s <ip|hostname> | -l

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B secret
is a program for transferring encrypted files using ICMP and ICMPv6
Echo-Request/Echo-Reply messages. Both IPv4 and IPv6 are supported.

Before transfer, files are encrypted using the AES-256 algorithm.
The program operates in a client-server mode: the client sends the encrypted file,
the server listens and saves the received decrypted file

This program requires root privileges for sending and receiving ICMP/ICMPv6 packets using
raw sockets.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r <file>
Specifies the file to be transferred by relative or absolute path.

.TP
.B \-s <ip|hostname>
IPv4 or IPv6 address or hostname of the server to which the file will be sent.

.TP
.B \-l
Server mode. Listens for incoming ICMP/ICMPv6 packets, reconstructs the
received data, decrypts it and saves the output file to the current
working directory.

.SH PROTOCOL OVERVIEW
The
.B secret
application protocol stores its data inside the payload of ICMP/ICMPv6
Echo-Request and Echo-Reply messages.

.P
After the ICMP/ICMPv6 header, every protocol packet begins with a
16-bit message type (network byte order).

.P
Supported message types:

.IP \[bu] 2
HELLO \- authenticate message containing the file name to be transferred.

.IP \[bu] 2
HELLO_ACK \- acknowledges for HELLO message.

.IP \[bu] 2
DATA \- contains an encrypted block for the file being transferred.

.IP \[bu] 2
DATA_ACK \- acknowledges for DATA message.

.IP \[bu] 2
FIN \- indicates the end of transmission from the client.

.IP \[bu] 2
FIN_ACK \- confirms for FIN message.

.IP \[bu] 2
FIN_ERR \- indicates an error occurred during file transfer from the server side.

.P
Message structure for HELLO and DATA:

.IP \[bu] 2
2 bytes \- message type  
.IP \[bu] 2
4 bytes \- size of encrypted data  
.IP \[bu] 2
N bytes \- encrypted data block  
.IP \[bu] 2
16 bytes \- AES initialization vector (IV)  
.IP \[bu] 2
4 bytes \- checksum of payload 

.P
Message structure for HELLO_ACK, DATA_ACK, FIN, FIN_ACK and FIN_ERR:

.IP \[bu] 2
2 bytes \- message type  
.IP \[bu] 2
4 bytes \- checksum of payload 

.P


.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Successful execution.

.TP
1
Invalid command-line arguments or missing required options.

.TP
2
Protocol errors like dont acknowledged packets or failure of transfer the file.

.TP
3
Internal error including encryption/decryption failure or socket errors.

.SH EXAMPLES
Start client and send a file:
.B secret -r images/image.png -s 10.10.10.115

Start server:
.B secret -l

